# An omen card may be cast as its Omen wherever a permission lets the card be cast (CR 601.3, 720.3), on the permission's
# terms. Bot1's Robber of the Rich attacks on turn 1 (haste) while Bot2 holds more cards, and exiles the top card of Bot2's
# library, Bot2's Twinmaw Stormbrood; Bot1 attacked with a Rogue this turn, so it may cast that card, spending mana as
# though it were mana of any color. In the second main phase Bot1 casts it as Charring Bite for {1}{R} paid with a Mox
# Sapphire and a Mox Jet - no red at all - at its own Robber, the only creature without flying. The Robber dies, and the
# Bite is shuffled into its owner's library, Bot2's (CR 720.3d): back to the eight cards Bot2's library had before the
# exile. Bot1's library is untouched and nothing is left in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Robber of the Rich
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Island
Island x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Twinmaw Stormbrood
Island x7

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Robber of the Rich.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
[T1 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Robber of the Rich > Bot2)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Exile = Twinmaw Stormbrood
? Bot2.Library.Count = 7
Bot1.Exile.Twinmaw Stormbrood.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Robber of the Rich; Ability: Omen)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
? Stack = Charring Bite
[T1 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Robber of the Rich
Bot2.Library.Count = 8
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 8
Bot2.Life = 18
